  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lucha contra la impunidad y construcci&#xf3;n de paz con justicia social en Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to join forces in the fight against impunity by making state criminality visible, identifying the differential impacts of socio-political violence and socio-environmental and ecological conflicts before national and international bodies. Promoting the clarification of the historical and judicial truth about political violence.&#xa0;
Regarding the work in territorial defence and the fight against the climate crisis, the project seeks the activation of justice in national and international jurisdiction in the face of human, territorial and environmental rights violations against communities, the strengthening of knowledge and skills of organisational processes and communities for the enforceability of collective rights in the protection of territory, health, the environment and nature.&#xa0;
With regard to work on overcoming conflict and peacebuilding, the aim is to promote institutional reforms that promote a drug policy in accordance with UN guidelines and international standards; the normative implementation of point 1 (rural reform), point 3 (protection guarantees for communities), point 4 (crop substitution) and point 6 (drug policy) of the Peace Agreement, with a comprehensive approach.&#xa0; Likewise, the promotion of the implementation of the normative and political framework on the comprehensive protection of human rights leaders and defenders and their work in defence of human rights and advocacy and communication actions to increase national and international social support for human rights leaders and defenders and the right to social protest.
With regard to the strengthening of the communications strategy, the project contemplates a long-range, public, popular, alternative and digital communications strategy through constant publications on CAJAR&apos;s social networks, press releases aimed at national and international media, interviews with the media, updates to the website and distribution of educational materials for the communities in the territory.</narrative>
  </description>
